---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const mail='mailto:katie@wyrd.team';
const projects=[
  {name:'Tavern Playhouse',file:'tavern-playhouse.app',note:'A TTRPG companion app designed to assist GMs in creating visuals for scenes in their games in which their players can be more immersed with theater of the mind elements of the game. With this players can follow along easier between NPC interactions and location changes, giving GMs a tool they can fall back on when scenes become complicated to explain and explore. This is the first application I made as the sole developer with the assistance of AI agents, learning both new skills as a developer and delving into the world of AI in the use of software development. While the application codebase was made by the agent, all of the art assets shown in the preview were made by me personally as a way to explore the app and how much a user may be able to push it using their own art.',image:'/projects/tavern-playhouse.png',alt:'Tavern Playhouse Performance Screen staging three actors in a library scene',width:1784,height:882,url:'https://playhouse.thetavern.app',action:'Explore Tavern Playhouse'},
  {name:"Cody’s Crayons",file:'codys-crayons.game',note:'A Slenderman-clone game made as a class project in university between myself and 5 other students for our final. I was the project manager and designed the AI that controls the enemy hunting you in the game. Through the 15 weeks we worked on the game, I came to learn better leadership and communication skills in order to organize, plan and coordinate the different parts of the work that went into this game. It was the first project that I also was able to put some of my software development skills into, and I was incredibly proud of the hard work that everyone (including myself) put in to get this project completed.',image:'/projects/codys-crayons.png',alt:"Cody’s Crayons gameplay inside a dark school computer lab",width:1322,height:1190,url:'https://iradesa.itch.io/codys-crayons',action:"Play Cody's Crayons"},
  {name:'Marion',file:'marion.game',note:'My first video game project in university, in which I worked with 7 other students to create a game by the end of the semester, while also presenting on sprints and development planning to showcase how we were working together as a development team. I was given the task of creating the initial concept and art for the entire game, which, as a hobbyist artist, was an exciting and challenging task. I had to coordinate meetings to ask for final designs and assets that were necessary for the development of the game, and complete the assets in a timely manner so the others had time to complete their tasks using my art. I learned how to take criticism and adjust my art to the work that was needed, and I was able to learn more about how assets for a 2D game were made, along with pixel art and animation. It was an incredibly fun project, and I hope one day I can revisit it to make it come to life even more than what was possible in only 15 weeks.',image:'/projects/marion.png',alt:'Main artwork for Marion showing a marionette suspended under a spotlight',width:1920,height:1080,secondaryImage:'/projects/marion-gameplay.png',secondaryAlt:'Marion gameplay showing the player facing an enemy inside a wooden dungeon room',secondaryWidth:1676,secondaryHeight:938,url:'https://github.com/BatesThaBeast/The-Labyrinth-Studios/tree/Main',action:'Play Marion'}
];
const tools=['Adobe Photoshop','AI agents','C++','CSS','Docker','Figma','GitHub','Go','HTML','Java','JavaScript','Python','Unity 5','Unreal Engine'];
const education='My path started with a B.S. in Computer Systems, focused on Game Development, from California State University of San Bernardino. I followed it with Google’s UX/UI Design Certificate, and I’m still adding new languages and software skills through Boot.dev.';
---
<SiteLayout>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#cbb8e8]">
    <header class="flex min-h-12 items-center justify-between gap-3 bg-[#704da0] px-4 text-xs text-white sm:px-6">
      <span class="flex gap-2" aria-hidden="true"><i class="size-3 rounded-full bg-[#ff8b78]"></i><i class="size-3 rounded-full bg-[#ffe16d]"></i><i class="size-3 rounded-full bg-[#aaff7a]"></i></span>
      <span>katelynlangley.dev</span><span>STILL LEARNING <b class="blink">●</b></span>
    </header>
    <div class="grid min-h-[calc(100vh-3rem)] gap-4 p-4 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_.9fr] lg:items-start lg:p-6">
      <section class="window flex flex-col bg-[#09170e] lg:sticky lg:top-6 lg:min-h-[calc(100vh-6rem)]"><div class="bar">about-katelyn-langley.txt</div><div class="flex flex-1 flex-col justify-between p-7 sm:p-10 lg:p-14"><div><h1 class="max-w-3xl font-grotesk text-[clamp(3.6rem,7vw,6rem)] font-bold leading-[.86] tracking-[-.04em] text-white">Hello! ･°˖✧◝(⁰▿⁰)◜✧˖°.</h1><p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[#a8c2aa]">My name is Katelyn Langley, and I'm a Junior Software Developer currently searching for full-time work while I do personal projects on the side. Most of what I know has come from making: trying an idea, getting stuck, finding a way through, and carrying that lesson into whatever I build next. Feel free to check out the projects showcased here and continue to follow this site as I continue to make and publish more projects in the future. Also consider reaching out to me using the button below to discuss anything about my work and future as a developer!</p><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-6 text-[#78907c]">{education}</p><a href={mail} class="mt-8 inline-block bg-[#baff70] px-5 py-3 font-bold text-[#102417] transition hover:bg-white">Come say hello (ᵔᵕᵔ)ﾉ →</a></div><div class="mt-12"><p class="mb-4 text-xs text-[#78907c]">WHAT I’M BUILDING WITH LATELY</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">{tools.map(t=><span class="rounded-md border border-[#52705a] px-3 py-2 text-xs">{t}</span>)}</div></div></div></section>
      <section class="grid gap-4" aria-label="Featured projects">{projects.map(p=><article class="window grid bg-[#d4e8dc] text-[#102417]"><div class="bar flex items-center justify-between gap-4"><span>{p.file}</span><span class="text-[#baff70]">PROJECT OPEN</span></div>{p.secondaryImage ? <div class="grid bg-[#050b18] sm:grid-cols-2"><img src={p.image} alt={p.alt} width={p.width} height={p.height} class="aspect-video h-full w-full object-cover object-top"/><img src={p.secondaryImage} alt={p.secondaryAlt} width={p.secondaryWidth} height={p.secondaryHeight} class="aspect-video h-full w-full object-cover object-top"/></div> : <img src={p.image} alt={p.alt} width={p.width} height={p.height} class="aspect-[2/1] w-full bg-[#050b18] object-cover object-top"/>}<div class="p-5"><h2 class="font-grotesk text-3xl font-bold">{p.name}</h2><p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5">{p.note}</p><a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-4 inline-block font-bold text-[#65438f] underline underline-offset-4">{p.action} →</a></div></article>)}</section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .window{overflow:hidden;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 20px 50px rgba(9,23,14,.24)}
  .bar{min-height:2.25rem;background:#704da0;color:white;padding:.65rem 1rem;font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.03em}
</style>
